  """
    Checks whether the tenant's Overview dashboard is on the latest enabled template version and,
    if it is behind, starts the upgrade in the background before answering.
  
  Called once per Workbench Overview page load by every user, so it is idempotent: it writes
    nothing when the dashboard is already current, and never starts a second upgrade while one is
    running. AVS resolves the vertical's Overview template and `DEFAULT` view itself; the client does
    not pass a view id or a template name.
  
  Callers who cannot manage the vertical receive the response without an upgrade being started, rather
    than an error. Every failure is silent to the user.
  
  Contract: https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~63da235fc2b1cb6b347016cf/pages/7846779679
  
  ### The field is not available for OAuth authenticated requests
  
  ### Field lifecycle
  
  This field is in the 'EXPERIMENTAL' lifecycle stage
  
  To query this field a client will need to add the '@optIn(to: "AssetsVerticalUpgradeOverviewDashboard")' query directive to the 'assetsVertical_upgradeOverviewDashboard' field, or to any of its parents.
  
