  """
    Updates the custom auth configuration of an already-registered MCP server.
  
  Rejects an authType that differs from the server's current one, and rejects values for inputs the
    admin does not own: inputs collected elsewhere in the registration flow, and values the platform
    derives rather than asks for.
  
  Requires the client secret on every edit whenever the provider requires one: it cannot be read
    back, and the provider configuration is replaced rather than patched, so accepting its absence
    would clear it.
  
  Where an update changes the endpoints consent was granted against, the response carries a consent
    URL: the provider will not honour tokens issued against different endpoints, so reporting success
    without re-consent would leave a silently broken connection.
  
  ### OAuth Scopes
  
  One of the following scopes will need to be present on OAuth requests to get data from this field
  
  * __manage:org__
  
  ### Field lifecycle
  
  This field is in the 'EXPERIMENTAL' lifecycle stage
  
  To query this field a client will need to add the '@optIn(to: "GraphIntegrationMcpAdminManagementMutation")' query directive to the 'graphIntegration_mcpAdminManagementUpdateMcpServerAuthConfig' field, or to any of its parents.
  
  The field is extremely unstable. It can go through changes at any moment, and its execution can be slow and/or unreliable. Clients should use it with care and at their own risk!
