  """
  Fetch agent evaluation response rows for a given Jira project, scoped to the
  tenant resolved from request `tenantId`, or from the `Atl-CloudId` request
  header when `tenantId` is omitted.
  
  - `projectId` (required): Jira project ID to scope the query.
  - `tenantId` (optional): Atlassian cloud ID / tenant ID to scope the query.
  When provided, it takes precedence over the GraphQL context and is validated
  against TCS before use.
  - `evaluationType` (optional): when omitted, returns rows for every evaluation type
  for the (tenantId, projectId) pair. When provided, returns rows only for that
  evaluation type.
  - `first` (optional): page size. Defaults to 25, capped at 200. Values outside
  `[1, 200]` are clamped.
  - `after` (optional): opaque pagination cursor returned as `nextPageToken` from
  the previous call. Omit (or pass null) to fetch the first page.
  
  Returns `QueryError` if cloudId is missing, request `tenantId` cannot be
  validated in TCS, or the underlying ERS lookup fails.
  
