  """
  Retrieve comment threads by their ARIs in a single batched request, each hydrated with the calling
  user's read state; backs the default hydration of `AVPCommentThread`. A thread is returned only if
  the caller can read the dashboard it belongs to, directly or through one of its charts. Threads
  that do not exist or cannot be read are omitted rather than reported, so the result may be shorter
  than `ids`; match results to requests by `id`, not by position. All ARIs must belong to the same
  workspace, and at most 25 may be requested: each thread costs a read-state lookup, an unread count,
  and a further page of comments if `comments` is selected.
  
