  """
    The user-authored ("custom") template gallery for a tenant, as a Relay connection. This is the
    only read surface for custom templates — the side-panel list and the full gallery are the same
    field with different arguments, and individual templates are read from the client's normalised
    store rather than by id.
  
  Requires site access; custom templates are visible to the whole tenant, so there is no per-row
    permission check.
  
  ### OAuth Scopes
  
  One of the following scopes will need to be present on OAuth requests to get data from this field
  
  * __jira:atlassian-external__
  """
  avp_getCustomTemplates(
    "Opaque cursor returned from a previous page's pageInfo.endCursor; omit for the first page."
    after: String,
    cloudId: ID! @CloudID(owner : "any"),
    "Only return templates reading from this data source."
    datasourceType: AVPTemplateDatasourceType,
    "Maximum number of edges to return in this page (capped server-side at 250)."
    first: Int!,
    """
    Case-insensitive match on the start of the template title. This is a prefix match, not a
    substring match: `titleLower` is the range key of the indexes serving this query, so ERS can
    serve `begins_with` but not `contains`.
    """
    search: String,
    "The workspace ARI of the consumer product, used as the ERS partition key for shard routing."
    workspaceAri: ID! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "any", type : "workspace", usesActivationId : true)
  ): AVPCustomTemplateConnection @rateLimited(disabled : false, rate : 20, usePerIpPolicy : false, usePerUserPolicy : true) @rateLimited(disabled : false, rate : 50, usePerIpPolicy : false, usePerUserPolicy : false) @scopes(product : JIRA, required : [JIRA_ATLASSIAN_EXTERNAL])
  "Retrieve a single dashboard by its ARI, including its charts, settings, and env vars."
  avp_getDashboard(dashboardAri: ID! @ARI(interpreted : false, owner : "avp", type : "dashboard", usesActivationId : false)): AVPDashboard @apiGroup(name : AVP) @rateLimited(disabled : false, rate : 60, usePerIpPolicy : false, usePerUserPolicy : true) @rateLimited(disabled : false, rate : 700, usePerIpPolicy : false, usePerUserPolicy : false)
  """
    For each chart on the dashboard, return the IDs of the dashboard env vars that the chart
    references — covering settings interpolation (`title` / `subtitle`), body content for
    `text` / `link` / `rich_text` charts, the pipeline SQL of every query on the chart's pipeline,
    the pipeline's node DAG (`formula` / `edit_column` / `filter` / `add_column_case_statement`), and
    the chart's own env var when the chart is itself a control (categorical dropdown, calendar,
    slider, etc.).
  
  The outer list has one entry per chart and follows `AVPDashboard.charts` iteration order. The
    inner `envVarIds` list is deduplicated and sorted by env var name for stable, cache-friendly
    output. Identifiers referenced anywhere that do not resolve to a dashboard env var are silently
    dropped (matches the Castle behaviour).
  
  Charts that have no pipeline, no settings, and no own env var appear with an empty `envVarIds`
    list.
  
  Requires at least READ access on the dashboard.
  
  ### OAuth Scopes
  
  One of the following scopes will need to be present on OAuth requests to get data from this field
  
  * __jira:atlassian-external__
  
  ### Field lifecycle
  
  This field is in the 'EXPERIMENTAL' lifecycle stage
  
  To query this field a client will need to add the '@optIn(to: "AVP-chart-used-env-vars")' query directive to the 'avp_getDashboardChartUsedEnvVars' field, or to any of its parents.
  
