  """
  List the repositories connected to the site where the calling user is a repository or workspace admin on the given
  provider. Admin rights come from the SCM provider; the user does not need to be a Jira site admin.
  Without workspaceUrl, returns every repository in connected workspaces the user administers, and the repositories
  the user is a Repo Admin of in the other connected workspaces. With workspaceUrl of a workspace the user administers,
  returns every repository in it. With workspaceUrl of another connected workspace, returns only its repositories the
  user is a Repo Admin of.
  GitHub repositories are checked one by one, so a page can hold fewer than `first` repositories while
  `pageInfo.hasNextPage` is true. Keep paging with `pageInfo.endCursor`.
  Alias the query once per provider to fetch both in one request.
  A user who has not linked a GitHub account gets an empty list for `provider: GITHUB`.
  Error `extensions.code` values: BAD_REQUEST, FEATURE_NOT_ENABLED, and SCM_UNAVAILABLE when a Bitbucket, GitHub or
  settings lookup failed, so the list would be incomplete. SCM_UNAVAILABLE can be retried.
  
  ### Field lifecycle
  
  This field is in the 'EXPERIMENTAL' lifecycle stage
  
  To query this field a client will need to add the '@optIn(to: "DevAiScmAdmin")' query directive to the 'devai_scmAdminRepositories' field, or to any of its parents.
  
  The field is extremely unstable. It can go through changes at any moment, and its execution can be slow and/or unreliable. Clients should use it with care and at their own risk!
  """
  devai_scmAdminRepositories(
    "Opaque cursor returned by a previous response. Pass it unchanged to continue pagination."
    after: String,
    cloudId: ID! @CloudID(owner : "jira"),
    "Maximum number of repositories to return, between 1 and 100."
    first: Int = 25,
    "`false`: only repositories without their own Code Reviewer settings. `true`: only repositories with them."
    hasOwnSettings: Boolean,
    provider: DevAiScmAdminProvider!,
    "Filters repositories by name. Passed through to the provider."
    search: String,
    "URL of a connected workspace (GitHub organisation or Bitbucket workspace) to list repositories from."
    workspaceUrl: URL
  ): DevAiScmAdminRepositoryConnection @lifecycle(allowThirdParties : false, name : "DevAiScmAdmin", stage : EXPERIMENTAL)
  """
  List the workspaces (GitHub organisations or Bitbucket workspaces) connected to the site where the calling user is
  a workspace admin on the given provider. Admin rights come from the SCM provider; the user does not need to be a
  Jira site admin. Only workspaces connected at the SCM connector level are returned.
  Alias the query once per provider to fetch both in one request.
  A user who has not linked a GitHub account gets an empty list for `provider: GITHUB`.
  Error `extensions.code` values: BAD_REQUEST, FEATURE_NOT_ENABLED, and SCM_UNAVAILABLE when a Bitbucket, GitHub or
  settings lookup failed, so the list would be incomplete. SCM_UNAVAILABLE can be retried.
  
  ### Field lifecycle
  
  This field is in the 'EXPERIMENTAL' lifecycle stage
  
  To query this field a client will need to add the '@optIn(to: "DevAiScmAdmin")' query directive to the 'devai_scmAdminWorkspaces' field, or to any of its parents.
  
  The field is extremely unstable. It can go through changes at any moment, and its execution can be slow and/or unreliable. Clients should use it with care and at their own risk!
  """
  devai_scmAdminWorkspaces(
    "Opaque cursor returned by a previous response. Pass it unchanged to continue pagination."
    after: String,
    cloudId: ID! @CloudID(owner : "jira"),
    "Maximum number of workspaces to return, between 1 and 100."
    first: Int = 25,
    provider: DevAiScmAdminProvider!
  ): DevAiScmAdminWorkspaceConnection @lifecycle(allowThirdParties : false, name : "DevAiScmAdmin", stage : EXPERIMENTAL)
