  """
  Fetches the dimensions for the directory items for the given DirectoryItemType
  
  ### OAuth Scopes
  
  One of the following scopes will need to be present on OAuth requests to get data from this field
  
  * __read:me__
  
  ### Field lifecycle
  
  This field is in the 'EXPERIMENTAL' lifecycle stage
  
  To query this field a client will need to add the '@optIn(to: "GraphIntegrationDimensionsQuery")' query directive to the 'graphIntegration_componentDirectoryDimensions' field, or to any of its parents.
  
  The field is extremely unstable. It can go through changes at any moment, and its execution can be slow and/or unreliable. Clients should use it with care and at their own risk!
  """
  graphIntegration_componentDirectoryDimensions(
    after: String,
    cloudId: ID! @CloudID,
    """
      Selected filter chips, using the same namespaced form this query returns — e.g.
      `integration:jira`, `tag:ai`, `capability:automation`, or a Product ARI on the MCP_SERVER rail.
      The auth filter is expressed the same way, as `authType:VALUE` where VALUE is a
      DirectoryAuthType: `authType:NONE`, `authType:OAUTH`, `authType:CLIENT_CREDENTIALS`,
      `authType:API_TOKEN`. It combines with a chip selection by AND. Auth is deliberately NOT surfaced
      as a dimension of its own, so `authType:*` is accepted as input while this query never returns one.
      Within one auth dimension id, separate DirectoryAuthType values with `|` to match ANY listed
      mechanism — e.g. `authType:NONE|API_TOKEN` matches NONE (no auth) or API_TOKEN, and
      `authType:OAUTH|CLIENT_CREDENTIALS` matches either OAuth mechanism. Items continue to report
      their actual auth mechanism. Separate dimension ids retain their existing AND semantics.
      Pipe-separated matching requires the tenant-scoped `enable-directory-auth-type-any-filter` gate.
      When disabled, auth values use exact matching, so a pipe-separated value matches nothing.
      This auth-only pipe syntax is an interim contract and may change as directory queries gain more
      operators across dimension types. Consumers must evolve alongside changes to this contract.
    
    On the MCP rails, pass at most one auth dimension id, which may contain pipe-separated values.
      Multiple auth ids remain unsupported and return an empty result rather than an error. Unknown
      or empty auth values match no mechanism; a filter containing only such values returns an empty
      result, so a filter is never silently dropped. On the ACTION rail, each auth dimension must match
      at least one declared mechanism, so separate auth ids are ANDed.
    
    Only dimensions leading to at least one matching item survive, so a returned dimension always
      leads to a non-empty items page for the same filter. MCP_TOOL dimensions are MCP servers, matched
      on their own auth type; MCP_SERVER dimensions are Product ARIs, kept when any server backing the
      Product ARI matches; ACTION dimensions are tags, capabilities and integrations, kept when any
      action behind them matches. Honoured on the MCP_SERVER, MCP_TOOL and ACTION rails; the skill rails
      have no auth, so an `authType:` id does not narrow their chips.
      A chip selection passed here does not narrow the chip rail it came from — only an `authType:` id
      does.
    """
    dimensionIds: [ID!],
    first: Int = 50,
    relevantFor: [GraphIntegrationDirectoryItemType!],
    surface: GraphIntegrationSurface
  ): GraphIntegrationDirectoryFilterDimensionConnection @apiGroup(name : ACTIONS) @lifecycle(allowThirdParties : false, name : "GraphIntegrationDimensionsQuery", stage : EXPERIMENTAL) @scopes(product : NO_GRANT_CHECKS, required : [READ_ME])
  """
