  The field is extremely unstable. It can go through changes at any moment, and its execution can be slow and/or unreliable. Clients should use it with care and at their own risk!
  """
  graphIntegration_componentDirectoryItems(
    after: String,
    """
    Keeps only items that support at least one of the given auth mechanisms. Omit (or pass an
    empty list) to apply no auth filtering. MCP tools are matched on their server's auth type.
    Honoured for MCP_SERVER and MCP_TOOL only. Every other item type accepts the argument and ignores
    it, so a page returned for ACTION, FORGE_TOOL or a skill type is unfiltered even when this is set
    — filter those rails with an `authType:VALUE` entry in dimensionIds instead.
    Note the asymmetry with the dimensions query, which takes its auth filter as an `authType:VALUE`
    dimension id instead: items are a flat list with no chip vocabulary, so a typed argument is the
    natural shape here.
    """
    authTypes: [GraphIntegrationDirectoryAuthType!],
    cloudId: ID! @CloudID,
    """
    Optional context ARI (platform site or Help Center) that owns the skills. When set, skill discovery
    is scoped to that context; when omitted, providers fall back to the platform site ARI derived from
    cloudId, preserving the existing site-scoped behaviour.
    """
    contextAri: ID,
    dimensionIds: [ID!],
    first: Int = 100,
    relevantFor: [GraphIntegrationDirectoryItemType!],
    searchKeyword: String,
    siteAri: ID,
    surface: GraphIntegrationSurface,
    tags: [String!]
  ): GraphIntegrationDirectoryItemConnection @apiGroup(name : ACTIONS) @lifecycle(allowThirdParties : true, name : "GraphIntegrationItemsQuery", stage : EXPERIMENTAL) @scopes(product : NO_GRANT_CHECKS, required : [READ_ME])
