  """
  The supported connectors available to the tenant, with the calling user's authorisation state
  against each, so a caller can tell whether a connector-dependent step will work before running it
  and where to send the user when it will not. Google Drive and SharePoint today; a tenant may have
  other Rovo connectors configured, and those are filtered out rather than reported, so this is not a
  complete inventory. Within that set, only connectors the tenant has configured are returned — an
  absent connector is not an unconnected one. `connectors` is empty for a tenant with none of them, and
  the query fails with `errorType: "CONNECTOR_SERVICE_ERROR"` when the provider cannot be read — an
  empty list is never used to stand in for "we could not tell". The name is capability-neutral so
  further connectors can be folded in later without a second query.
  
  ### Field lifecycle
  
  This field is in the 'EXPERIMENTAL' lifecycle stage
  
  To query this field a client will need to add the '@optIn(to: "PlaybooksInJSM")' query directive to the 'playbook_unifiedConnectors' field, or to any of its parents.
  
  The field is extremely unstable. It can go through changes at any moment, and its execution can be slow and/or unreliable. Clients should use it with care and at their own risk!
  """
  playbook_unifiedConnectors(cloudId: ID! @CloudID(owner : "jira")): PlaybookUnifiedConnectorsQueryPayload @lifecycle(allowThirdParties : false, name : "PlaybooksInJSM", stage : EXPERIMENTAL)
